  "title": "Kirby Problem 4.3",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Are there exotic smooth structures on the following closed, simply-connected 4–manifolds?\n\n(a) $\\#_{k}\\mathbb{CP}^{2}$ for any $k \\geq$ 1.\n\n(b) $\\#_{m}(\\mathbb{CP}^{2}\\#\\overline{\\mathbb{CP}}{}^{2})$ and $\\#_{n}(S^{2} \\times S^{2})$ for $m \\leq$ 8, $n \\leq$ 10.\n\n(c) $\\#_{p}K3 \\#_{q}(S^{2} \\times S^{2})$ for any $p \\geq$ q+5. If so, what are the smallest k, m and n? The largest p and q?",
